---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Whose Lamb Is It? — Daf Yomi Game: Bekhorot 11"
  description="Bekhorot 11: count out the coins Rabbi Tarfon asked for, pass lambs, donkeys and grain piles from hand to hand and decide who ends up holding them, then unlock why Rav Naḥman needed both of his inheritance rulings."
>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Frank+Ruhl+Libre:wght@400;500;700;900&display=swap"
  />

  <main class="frank min-h-screen bg-[#191b17] !text-[#ece6d6]">
    <!-- ============ Hero ============ -->
    <header class="px-4 pt-12 pb-8">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-sm !text-[#a3a08f]">
          <a href="/daf" class="underline decoration-[#4a4a3a] hover:!text-[#d4ad55]">Daf Yomi Arcade</a>, Bekhorot 11, 5 October 2026
        </p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 text-5xl font-black leading-[1.05] sm:text-6xl">Whose Lamb Is It?</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-2xl !text-[#d4ad55]" dir="rtl" lang="he">עַיִן יָפָה בְּסֶלַע, עַיִן רָעָה בְּשֶׁקֶל, בֵּינוֹנִית בְּרִגְיָא</p>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc8b4]">
          A firstborn donkey is redeemed with a lamb that goes to a kohen. Today's daf asks how much that lamb
          has to be worth, and then follows lambs, donkeys and piles of grain as they pass from hand to hand:
          through a stranger, a thief, a kohen grandfather, a gentile seller. At the end of each chain, someone is
          holding it. Your job is to say who.
        </p>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 600 70" class="mt-6 w-full" aria-hidden="true">
          <line x1="10" y1="54" x2="590" y2="54" stroke="#4a4a3a" stroke-width="2" />
          <g fill="#8c8a86">
            <ellipse cx="70" cy="36" rx="24" ry="11" />
            <rect x="52" y="42" width="5" height="12" /><rect x="82" y="42" width="5" height="12" />
            <path d="M91 30 L106 16 L114 20 L100 36 Z" />
            <path d="M106 16 L104 5 L109 14 Z M110 17 L112 6 L114 16 Z" />
          </g>
          <path d="M140 40 Q 300 0 460 40" fill="none" stroke="#d4ad55" stroke-dasharray="4 6" stroke-width="1.5" />
          <g fill="#ece6d6">
            <circle cx="300" cy="22" r="8" /><circle cx="291" cy="26" r="7" /><circle cx="309" cy="26" r="7" />
          </g>
          <g fill="#ece6d6">
            <ellipse cx="520" cy="40" rx="17" ry="10" />
            <circle cx="538" cy="34" r="6" />
            <rect x="508" y="46" width="3" height="8" fill="#a3a08f" /><rect x="528" y="46" width="3" height="8" fill="#a3a08f" />
          </g>
          <text x="300" y="64" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#a3a08f">who is holding it?</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pb-20">
      <!-- ============ Part I: the purse ============ -->
      <section class="border-t border-[#3a3a2e] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p1">
        <h2 id="p1" class="text-3xl font-bold">I. Count out the lamb</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc8b4]">
          Rabbi Yehuda Nesia sent his firstborn donkey to Rabbi Tarfon and asked how much he had to give the kohen.
          The rulings are in coins: a <strong>sela</strong> is 4 dinars, a <strong>shekel</strong> is 2, and a
          <strong>ma'a</strong> (<span dir="rtl" lang="he">דַּנְקָא</span>) is a sixth of a dinar. Tap coins into the purse
          (tap a coin in the purse to take it back), then hand it over.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-2" role="group" aria-label="Coins">
          <button class="coin" data-c="sela">◉ Sela <span class="!text-[#a3a08f]">4 dinars</span></button>
          <button class="coin" data-c="shekel">◉ Shekel <span class="!text-[#a3a08f]">2</span></button>
          <button class="coin" data-c="dinar">● Dinar <span class="!text-[#a3a08f]">1</span></button>
          <button class="coin" data-c="maa">· Ma'a <span class="!text-[#a3a08f]">⅙</span></button>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-[#3a3a2e] bg-[#20221d] p-4">
          <p id="purse-task" class="text-lg font-bold !text-[#d4ad55]"></p>
          <p id="purse-sub" class="mt-1 text-sm !text-[#cfc8b4]"></p>
          <div id="purse" class="mt-3 flex min-h-[2.75rem] flex-wrap gap-1.5" aria-live="polite" aria-label="Purse"></div>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm !text-[#a3a08f]">In the purse: <span id="purse-total" class="!text-[#ece6d6]">0</span></p>
          <div id="purse-alt" class="mt-3 hidden"></div>
          <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <button id="purse-give" class="act">Hand it over</button>
            <button id="purse-clear" class="act">Empty purse</button>
          </div>
          <div id="purse-fb" class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed" aria-live="polite"></div>
          <button id="purse-next" class="act mt-3 hidden">Next ▸</button>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Part II: the relay ============ -->
      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#3a3a2e] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p2">
        <h2 id="p2" class="text-3xl font-bold">II. Pass it along</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc8b4]">
          Each case is a chain of hands. Step the item along with <em>Pass</em> and read what happens at each hand.
          When it reaches the end, rule who ends up holding it.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-5 rounded-lg border border-[#3a3a2e] bg-[#20221d] p-4">
          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
            <p id="relay-title" class="text-lg font-bold !text-[#d4ad55]"></p>
            <p id="relay-count" class="shrink-0 text-sm !text-[#a3a08f]"></p>
          </div>
          <div id="track" class="track mt-4" aria-hidden="true">
            <div id="track-line" class="track-line"></div>
            <div id="hands" class="hands"></div>
            <div id="token" class="token"></div>
          </div>
          <p id="relay-cap" class="mt-4 min-h-[3rem] text-base leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc8b4]" aria-live="polite"></p>
          <button id="relay-pass" class="act mt-1">Pass ▸</button>
          <div id="relay-q" class="mt-3 hidden">
            <p id="relay-qtext" class="text-base font-bold !text-[#ece6d6]"></p>
            <div id="relay-opts" class="mt-2 grid gap-2"></div>
          </div>
          <div id="relay-fb" class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed" aria-live="polite"></div>
          <button id="relay-next" class="act mt-3 hidden">Next chain ▸</button>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Part III: the lock ============ -->
      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#3a3a2e] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p3">
        <h2 id="p3" class="text-3xl font-bold">III. Why say it twice?</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc8b4]">
          Rav Naḥman ruled the kohen-grandfather inheritance twice: once for donkeys, once for untithed grain.
          The Gemara says both were needed (<span dir="rtl" lang="he">וּצְרִיכָא</span>). Each ruling has a feature the
          other lacks. Set both dials to the real reasons and the lock opens.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-[#3a3a2e] bg-[#20221d] p-4">
            <p class="text-sm !text-[#a3a08f]">Had he taught only the donkeys, I'd say the grandson keeps the lambs only because…</p>
            <div id="dial-a" class="mt-3 grid gap-2" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Donkey-only reason"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-[#3a3a2e] bg-[#20221d] p-4">
            <p class="text-sm !text-[#a3a08f]">Had he taught only the grain, I'd say the grandson keeps the teruma only because…</p>
            <div id="dial-b" class="mt-3 grid gap-2" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Grain-only reason"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-4 flex items-center gap-3">
          <button id="lock-try" class="act">Try the lock</button>
          <span id="lock-icon" class="text-3xl" aria-hidden="true">🔒</span>
        </div>
        <div id="lock-fb" class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed" aria-live="polite"></div>
      </section>

      <div id="finale" class="mt-12 hidden rounded-lg border border-[#d4ad55]/40 p-6 text-center">
        <p class="text-3xl font-bold !text-[#d4ad55]" dir="rtl" lang="he">מֵעִידָּנָא דְּאַפְרְשֵׁיהּ, בִּרְשׁוּתֵיהּ דְּכֹהֵן קָאֵי</p>
        <p id="finale-text" class="mt-2 text-base !text-[#cfc8b4]"></p>
      </div>

      <!-- ============ Learn the real daf ============ -->
      <div class="mt-14 border-t border-[#3a3a2e] pt-8">
        <h3 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#d4ad55]">Learn the real daf</h3>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc8b4]">
          Bekhorot 11 settles the value of the redemption lamb (any amount after the fact, a ragya if you ask),
          allows redeeming with money or goods worth the donkey, and proves from the thief's double payment that a
          firstborn donkey isn't treated like Temple property. It then follows Rav Naḥman's rulings in the name of
          Rabba bar Avuh about doubtful and inherited firstborn donkeys and untithed grain, Rabbi Ḥanina on smoothed
          grain piles bought from a gentile, and the Demai mishna about produce left with a gentile.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-sm">
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.11a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#d4ad55]/50 px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#d4ad55] hover:border-[#d4ad55]">Bekhorot 11 on Sefaria ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Bekhorot.11a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a3a2e] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a3a08f] hover:border-[#d4ad55]">Rashi ×45 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Steinsaltz_on_Bekhorot.11a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a3a2e] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a3a08f] hover:border-[#d4ad55]">Steinsaltz ×37 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rabbeinu_Gershom_on_Bekhorot.11a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a3a2e] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a3a08f] hover:border-[#d4ad55]">Rabbeinu Gershom ×32 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Bekhorot.11a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a3a2e] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a3a08f] hover:border-[#d4ad55]">Tosafot ×11 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Demai.3.4" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a3a2e] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a3a08f] hover:border-[#d4ad55]">Mishna Demai 3:4 ↗</a>
          <span class="rounded-full border border-[#3a3a2e] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a3a08f]">Sefer Mitzvot Gadol ×13</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 text-sm !text-[#7a7766]">
          Part of the <a href="/daf" class="underline decoration-[#4a4a3a] hover:!text-[#a3a08f]">Daf Yomi Arcade</a>,
          a new game from every daf. Texts and links via the Sefaria API.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <style is:global>
    .frank { font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; }
    .act, .coin, .opt {
      border-radius: 0.35rem;
      border: 1px solid #55554a;
      background: #191b17;
      color: #ece6d6;
      padding: 0.5rem 0.95rem;
      font-size: 1rem;
      transition: border-color 0.15s, background-color 0.15s;
    }
    .opt { text-align: left; }
    .coin { border-color: #7a6a3a; }
    .act:hover:not(:disabled), .coin:hover:not(:disabled), .opt:hover:not(:disabled) { border-color: #d4ad55; }
    .act:focus-visible, .coin:focus-visible, .opt:focus-visible, .chip:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #d4ad55; outline-offset: 2px; }
    .act:disabled, .coin:disabled, .opt:disabled { opacity: 0.55; cursor: default; }
    .opt[aria-checked='true'] { border-color: #d4ad55; background: #2c2a1c; }
    .ok { border-color: #8fae7a !important; background: #1f2a1c !important; }
    .bad { border-color: #b4553a !important; background: #2c1b15 !important; }
    .chip {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
      border-radius: 999px; background: #d4ad55; color: #191b17 !important;
      font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; padding: 0.25rem 0.6rem;
      animation: drop 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.3, 1.4, 0.6, 1);
    }
    .chip.small { background: #a8925a; }
    .track { position: relative; height: 92px; }
    .track-line { position: absolute; left: 6%; right: 6%; top: 26px; height: 2px; background: #3a3a2e; }
    .hands { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }
    .hand { width: 0; flex: 1; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 4px; text-align: center; }
    .hand .ico { width: 52px; height: 52px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid #3a3a2e; background: #191b17; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 1.5rem; }
    .hand.here .ico { border-color: #d4ad55; }
    .hand .lbl { font-size: 0.72rem; line-height: 1.1; color: #a3a08f !important; max-width: 7rem; }
    .token { position: absolute; top: -6px; width: 28px; height: 28px; margin-left: -14px; border-radius: 999px; background: #ece6d6; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 1rem; box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px #191b17; transition: left 0.6s cubic-bezier(0.4, 1.3, 0.6, 1); }
    @keyframes drop { from { transform: translateY(-14px); opacity: 0; } to { transform: none; opacity: 1; } }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .chip { animation: none !important; }
      .token { transition: none !important; }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id)!;
    const sef = (ref: string) => `https://www.sefaria.org/${ref.replace(/ (\d+[ab]?):/, '.$1.').replace(/ /g, '_')}`;
    const link = (ref: string) =>
      `<a href="${sef(ref)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="!text-[#d4ad55] underline decoration-[#4a4a3a] hover:!text-[#f0d68a]">${ref} ↗</a>`;
    const good = (s: string) => `<p class="!text-[#b9d6a6]">✓ ${s}</p>`;
    const miss = (s: string) => `<p class="!text-[#f0c2b2]">✗ ${s}</p>`;
    const score = { purse: 0, relay: 0, lock: 0 };
    const done = { purse: false, relay: false, lock: false };

    // =============== PART I: the purse ===============
    // all values in ma'ot (1 dinar = 6 ma'ot)
    const COINS: Record<string, { v: number; name: string }> = {
      sela: { v: 24, name: 'Sela' },
      shekel: { v: 12, name: 'Shekel' },
      dinar: { v: 6, name: 'Dinar' },
      maa: { v: 1, name: "Ma'a" },
    };
    const fmt = (m: number) => {
      const d = Math.floor(m / 6), r = m % 6;
      if (!m) return '0';
      return [d ? `${d} dinar${d > 1 ? 's' : ''}` : '', r ? `${r} ma'a${r > 1 ? 'ot' : ''}` : ''].filter(Boolean).join(' + ');
    };
    type PurseRound = {
      task: string; sub: string; mode: 'exact' | 'min' | 'value'; target: number;
      alt?: boolean; hit: string; ref: string; wrong: (m: number) => string;
    };
    const ROUNDS: PurseRound[] = [
      {
        task: 'Rabbi Tarfon: the generous eye', sub: '"One with a generous disposition redeems with…" Put that amount in the purse.',
        mode: 'exact', target: 24, ref: 'Bekhorot 11a:4',
        hit: 'A sela, 4 dinars: the generous eye.',
        wrong: (m) => `That's ${fmt(m)}. The generous eye gives a sela: 4 dinars.`,
      },
      {
        task: 'Rabbi Tarfon: the miserly eye', sub: '"One with a miserly disposition redeems with…"',
        mode: 'exact', target: 12, ref: 'Bekhorot 11a:4',
        hit: 'A shekel, 2 dinars: the miserly eye.',
        wrong: (m) => `That's ${fmt(m)}. The miserly eye gives a shekel: 2 dinars.`,
      },
      {
        task: 'Rabbi Tarfon: the middle eye', sub: '"…and the intermediate one, with a ragya." Rava: the halakha is a ragya. How much is a ragya?',
        mode: 'exact', target: 18, ref: 'Bekhorot 11a:5',
        hit: 'Three dinars. It\'s called <em>ragya</em> because it is <span dir="rtl" lang="he">רְגִיל הָכָא וְרָגִיל הָכָא</span>, "near here and near there," right between the sela and the shekel.',
        wrong: (m) => `That's ${fmt(m)}. A ragya sits between the sela (4) and the shekel (2): three dinars.`,
      },
      {
        task: 'He already did it himself', sub: 'A man redeemed his donkey on his own, without asking, with a lean lamb (<em>patruza</em>). Fill the purse with the least that lamb can be worth and still count.',
        mode: 'min', target: 1, ref: 'Bekhorot 11a:6',
        hit: 'One ma\'a. Rav Naḥman rules like the Rabbis: any amount works, and Rav Yosef says even a lean lamb worth a ma\'a. So Rava\'s ragya and Rav Naḥman don\'t clash: a ragya for <em>one who comes to ask</em>, a ma\'a is enough for <em>one who acts on his own</em> (<span dir="rtl" lang="he">כָּאן בְּבָא לִימָּלֵךְ, כָּאן בְּעוֹשֶׂה מֵעַצְמוֹ</span>).',
        wrong: (m) => `${fmt(m)} works, but it isn't the least. After the fact any lamb counts: Rav Yosef allows a lean lamb worth only one ma'a.`,
      },
      {
        task: 'No lamb at all', sub: 'Reish Lakish: someone with no lamb can redeem with the donkey\'s value. This donkey is worth 2 selas and a shekel. Pay it in coins, or try what Rav Naḥman son of Rav Yosef used.',
        mode: 'value', target: 60, alt: true, ref: 'Bekhorot 11a:10',
        hit: 'Ten dinars, the donkey\'s full value. Ravina: this holds even for Rabbi Yehuda. A firstborn donkey can\'t be stricter than consecrated property, which is redeemed with anything worth its value. The Torah said "a lamb" to make it <em>easier</em>, since a lamb is worth less than a donkey. Rav Naḥman son of Rav Yosef redeemed his with boiled vegetables (<span dir="rtl" lang="he">שִׁילְקֵי</span>) worth the donkey.',
        wrong: (m) => `That's ${fmt(m)}. Without a lamb, the cheaper way is gone. You pay what the donkey is worth: 2 selas + a shekel = 10 dinars.`,
      },
    ];
    let ri = 0, purse: string[] = [], purseLocked = false, roundMissed = false;
    const renderPurse = () => {
      const total = purse.reduce((s, c) => s + COINS[c].v, 0);
      $('purse').innerHTML = purse.length
        ? purse.map((c, i) => `<button class="chip ${COINS[c].v < 6 ? 'small' : ''}" data-i="${i}" aria-label="Remove ${COINS[c].name}">${COINS[c].name}</button>`).join('')
        : '<span class="text-sm !text-[#7a7766]">empty</span>';
      $('purse-total').textContent = fmt(total);
      return total;
    };
    const loadRound = () => {
      const r = ROUNDS[ri];
      purse = []; purseLocked = false; roundMissed = false;
      $('purse-task').innerHTML = `${ri + 1}/${ROUNDS.length} · ${r.task}`;
      $('purse-sub').innerHTML = r.sub;
      $('purse-fb').innerHTML = '';
      $('purse-next').classList.add('hidden');
      ($('purse-give') as HTMLButtonElement).disabled = false;
      const alt = $('purse-alt');
      alt.classList.toggle('hidden', !r.alt);
      alt.innerHTML = r.alt ? `<button id="veg" class="act">🥬 A pot of boiled vegetables worth 10 dinars</button>` : '';
      if (r.alt) $('veg').addEventListener('click', () => finishRound(true, true));
      renderPurse();
    };
    const finishRound = (ok: boolean, veg = false) => {
      const r = ROUNDS[ri];
      if (ok) {
        purseLocked = true;
        if (!roundMissed) score.purse++;
        $('purse-fb').innerHTML = good((veg ? 'Goods work too. ' : '') + r.hit) + `<p class="mt-1 text-sm">${link(r.ref)}</p>`;
        ($('purse-give') as HTMLButtonElement).disabled = true;
        const next = $('purse-next');
        next.textContent = ri < ROUNDS.length - 1 ? 'Next ▸' : 'On to the relay ▸';
        next.classList.remove('hidden');
        next.focus();
      }
    };
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.coin').forEach((b) =>
      b.addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (purseLocked) return;
        purse.push(b.dataset.c!);
        renderPurse();
      }),
    );
    $('purse').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      const t = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLElement>('.chip');
      if (!t || purseLocked) return;
      purse.splice(Number(t.dataset.i), 1);
      renderPurse();
    });
    $('purse-clear').addEventListener('click', () => { if (!purseLocked) { purse = []; renderPurse(); } });
    $('purse-give').addEventListener('click', () => {
      const r = ROUNDS[ri];
      const total = renderPurse();
      if (!total) { $('purse-fb').innerHTML = miss('The purse is empty.'); return; }
      if (total === r.target) return finishRound(true);
      roundMissed = true;
      $('purse-fb').innerHTML = miss(r.wrong(total)) + '<p class="mt-1 text-sm !text-[#a3a08f]">Adjust the purse and try again.</p>';
    });
    $('purse-next').addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (ri < ROUNDS.length - 1) { ri++; loadRound(); return; }
      done.purse = true;
      $('purse-task').textContent = `Purse: ${score.purse}/${ROUNDS.length} right the first time`;
      $('purse-sub').textContent = 'Rabbi Tarfon\'s three eyes, Rava\'s ragya, Rav Yosef\'s lean lamb, and Reish Lakish\'s money in place of a lamb.';
      $('purse-next').classList.add('hidden');
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.coin').forEach((b) => (b.disabled = true));
      $('p2').scrollIntoView({ behavior: matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches ? 'auto' : 'smooth' });
      checkFinale();
    });
    loadRound();

    // =============== PART II: the relay ===============
    type Hand = { ico: string; lbl: string; cap: string };
    type Chain = { title: string; item: string; hands: Hand[]; q: string; opts: string[]; ans: number; why: string; ref: string };
    const CHAINS: Chain[] = [
      {
        title: 'Someone else redeems your donkey', item: '🐑',
        hands: [
          { ico: '🫏', lbl: 'Shimon\'s firstborn donkey', cap: 'Shimon owns a firstborn donkey and hasn\'t redeemed it.' },
          { ico: '🧔', lbl: 'Reuven, a stranger', cap: 'Reuven gives a kohen his own lamb for Shimon\'s donkey. Rav Huna: the donkey is redeemed.' },
          { ico: '❓', lbl: 'the redeemed donkey', cap: 'For Rabbi Shimon there\'s no question: the owner could use it all along. But for Rabbi Yehuda it was forbidden until now. Does whoever pays get it, as with consecrated property ("he gives the money and it is his")?' },
        ],
        q: 'Who owns the redeemed donkey?', opts: ['Reuven, who paid', 'Shimon, the owner', 'The kohen'], ans: 1,
        why: 'Rav Naḥman brings a baraita: someone who steals a firstborn donkey pays the double payment <em>to the owner</em>, who "has no rights to it now but will have them later." If it were like Temple property there would be no double payment: "stolen from the <em>man\'s</em> house," not from the Temple. So it isn\'t like consecrated property, and it stays Shimon\'s. <span dir="rtl" lang="he">וְתוּ לָא מִידֵּי</span>: nothing more to say.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 11a:16',
      },
      {
        title: 'Ten doubtful donkeys', item: '🐑',
        hands: [
          { ico: '🫏', lbl: '10 maybe-firstborn donkeys', cap: 'An Israelite has ten donkeys, each of which may or may not be a firstborn.' },
          { ico: '🐑', lbl: '10 lambs set aside', cap: 'He designates ten lambs to redeem them, one per doubt.' },
          { ico: '🚪', lbl: 'the tithe pen', cap: 'The mishna says such a lamb is tithed with his ordinary flock. Every tenth lamb through the gate is ma\'aser.' },
        ],
        q: 'After tithing, who has the lambs?', opts: ['A kohen gets all ten', 'He keeps them', 'A kohen gets one, he keeps nine'], ans: 1,
        why: 'He tithes them and they are his (<span dir="rtl" lang="he">וְהֵן שֶׁלּוֹ</span>). Each donkey is only <em>maybe</em> a firstborn, so a kohen can\'t prove his claim to any of the lambs. The baraita supports Rav Naḥman, who said this in the name of Rabba bar Avuh.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 11a:19',
      },
      {
        title: 'The lamb the kohen already has', item: '🐑',
        hands: [
          { ico: '🫏', lbl: 'a doubtful donkey', cap: 'Same doubtful case, but this time the lamb has been handed over.' },
          { ico: '🧑‍🦳', lbl: 'the kohen', cap: 'The lamb is now in the kohen\'s flock.' },
          { ico: '🚪', lbl: 'the tithe pen?', cap: 'The mishna on 55b: an animal you bought or got as a present is exempt from animal tithe.' },
        ],
        q: 'Does this lamb go through the kohen\'s tithe pen?', opts: ['Yes, like any lamb', 'No, it\'s exempt'], ans: 1,
        why: 'The lamb came to the kohen as a gift, and gifts are exempt from animal tithe. The baraita says the "enters the pen" ruling can\'t be about this case. It only applies to the Israelite who still holds his own lambs.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 11a:18',
      },
      {
        title: 'Donkeys through a kohen grandfather', item: '🫏',
        hands: [
          { ico: '👴', lbl: 'Israelite great-grandfather', cap: 'An Israelite owns ten certain firstborn donkeys. They need redemption.' },
          { ico: '🧑‍🦳', lbl: 'his daughter\'s son, a kohen', cap: 'They pass to his daughter\'s son, a kohen. He should have redeemed them, but he could have kept the lambs himself.' },
          { ico: '🧒', lbl: 'his daughter\'s son, an Israelite', cap: 'The kohen dies and the donkeys pass to <em>his</em> daughter\'s son, an Israelite.' },
        ],
        q: 'The grandson sets aside ten lambs and tithes them. Then?', opts: ['He gives them to a kohen', 'He keeps them', 'They are forbidden to everyone'], ans: 1,
        why: 'He keeps them, as if his kohen grandfather had set them aside, owned them, and left them to him. Rav Naḥman in the name of Rabba bar Avuh.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 11a:21',
      },
      {
        title: 'Grain through a kohen grandfather', item: '🌾',
        hands: [
          { ico: '👴', lbl: 'Israelite great-grandfather', cap: 'Smoothed piles of untithed grain (<em>tevel</em>): fully processed, so teruma and tithes are due.' },
          { ico: '🧑‍🦳', lbl: 'his daughter\'s son, a kohen', cap: 'Inherited by a kohen grandson, who never separated the gifts.' },
          { ico: '🧒', lbl: 'his daughter\'s son, an Israelite', cap: 'Inherited in turn by the kohen\'s Israelite grandson.' },
        ],
        q: 'The grandson separates teruma and tithes. Who gets them?', opts: ['A kohen and a Levite', 'He keeps them', 'He need not separate at all'], ans: 1,
        why: 'He separates, and they are his, as if the kohen grandfather had separated them, taken them, and left them to him. (Part III asks why Rav Naḥman needed to say this twice.)',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 11a:22',
      },
      {
        title: 'Piles bought from a gentile, smoothed by a gentile', item: '🌾',
        hands: [
          { ico: '🧑‍🌾', lbl: 'gentile grower', cap: 'A gentile grows grain in the Land of Israel.' },
          { ico: '🪵', lbl: 'gentile smooths the pile', cap: 'The gentile finishes processing: he smooths the pile.' },
          { ico: '🧔', lbl: 'Jewish buyer', cap: 'A Jew buys the finished pile.' },
        ],
        q: 'What does the buyer owe?', opts: ['Teruma and tithes, given away', 'Separate, but keep them', 'Nothing: not obligated'], ans: 2,
        why: '"<em>Your</em> grain": only grain whose processing a Jew completed is subject to teruma and tithes. So the Gemara concludes Rabbi Ḥanina must be talking about a pile a Jew smoothed.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 11b:2',
      },
      {
        title: 'Piles bought from a gentile, smoothed by a Jew', item: '🌾',
        hands: [
          { ico: '🧑‍🌾', lbl: 'gentile owner', cap: 'The grain is the gentile\'s, in the Land of Israel.' },
          { ico: '🧔', lbl: 'a Jew smooths it', cap: 'A Jew smooths the pile while it\'s still the gentile\'s. A gentile\'s ownership in the Land can\'t cancel the tithe obligation.' },
          { ico: '🛒', lbl: 'Jewish buyer', cap: 'A Jew buys it, as Rabbi Ḥanina describes.' },
        ],
        q: 'Rabbi Ḥanina rules:', opts: ['He tithes, and gives them away', 'He tithes, and they are his', 'Exempt entirely'], ans: 1,
        why: 'He tithes, and they are his. He can tell the kohen: "I come in the place of a man you can\'t take to court," the gentile, who owed you nothing. Abaye later cites Rabbi Yehoshua ben Levi: Numbers 18:26 says "when you take <em>from the children of Israel</em>," so produce bought from a gentile is exempt from teruma of the tithe.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 11b:3',
      },
      {
        title: 'Produce left with a Samaritan', item: '🧺',
        hands: [
          { ico: '🧔', lbl: 'owner', cap: 'An owner leaves his produce on deposit…' },
          { ico: '🧑', lbl: 'Samaritan or am ha\'aretz', cap: '…with a Samaritan or someone unreliable about tithes.' },
          { ico: '🧔', lbl: 'owner again', cap: 'They give it back.' },
        ],
        q: 'What is the returned produce?', opts: ['It keeps its earlier status', 'Treated as demai', 'Treated as the depositee\'s own produce'], ans: 0,
        why: 'It keeps its earlier status for tithes and for Sabbatical-year produce. They aren\'t suspected of swapping it.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 11b:4',
      },
      {
        title: 'Produce left with a gentile', item: '🧺',
        hands: [
          { ico: '🧔', lbl: 'owner', cap: 'An owner leaves produce with a gentile.' },
          { ico: '🧑‍🌾', lbl: 'gentile', cap: 'First tanna: treat it as the gentile\'s own, since he probably swapped it. Rabbi Shimon: it\'s demai, because maybe he swapped it and maybe he didn\'t.' },
          { ico: '🧔', lbl: 'owner again', cap: 'Rabbi Elazar: everyone agrees he must separate teruma and tithes from it.' },
        ],
        q: 'So according to Rabbi Elazar, what is the dispute about?', opts: ['Whether to separate at all', 'Whether to give what he separated to the kohen', 'Whether the gentile owns it'], ans: 1,
        why: 'Whether he gives it away. The first tanna: he gives the teruma to a kohen. Rabbi Shimon: as with demai, the kohen has to bring proof. Abaye asks how anyone could require giving, given Rabbi Ḥanina\'s "they are his." Rav Dimi answers that perhaps the mishna means teruma gedola, while Rabbi Ḥanina means teruma of the tithe.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 11b:8',
      },
      {
        title: 'The lamb that died on the way', item: '🐑',
        hands: [
          { ico: '🫏', lbl: 'firstborn donkey', cap: 'An Israelite redeems his firstborn donkey.' },
          { ico: '🐑', lbl: 'lamb set aside', cap: 'He sets aside the lamb. Before he can bring it to the kohen, it dies in his house.' },
          { ico: '🧑‍🦳', lbl: 'the kohen', cap: 'The mishna: "if it dies, one may benefit from it." But who?' },
        ],
        q: 'Who benefits from the dead lamb?', opts: ['The Israelite, since it never reached the kohen', 'The kohen', 'No one'], ans: 1,
        why: 'The kohen. You might think he doesn\'t acquire it until it reaches his hand. The mishna teaches that from the moment it was set aside, it stands in the kohen\'s possession.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 11b:11',
      },
    ];
    let ci = 0, step = 0;
    const placeToken = () => {
      const n = CHAINS[ci].hands.length;
      $('token').style.left = `${((step + 0.5) / n) * 100}%`;
      document.querySelectorAll('.hand').forEach((h, i) => h.classList.toggle('here', i === step));
    };
    const loadChain = () => {
      const c = CHAINS[ci];
      step = 0;
      $('relay-title').textContent = c.title;
      $('relay-count').textContent = `${ci + 1}/${CHAINS.length}`;
      $('hands').innerHTML = c.hands.map((h) => `<div class="hand"><div class="ico">${h.ico}</div><div class="lbl">${h.lbl}</div></div>`).join('');
      $('token').textContent = c.item;
      $('relay-cap').innerHTML = c.hands[0].cap;
      $('relay-q').classList.add('hidden');
      $('relay-fb').innerHTML = '';
      $('relay-next').classList.add('hidden');
      const pass = $('relay-pass') as HTMLButtonElement;
      pass.classList.remove('hidden');
      pass.disabled = false;
      placeToken();
    };
    $('relay-pass').addEventListener('click', () => {
      const c = CHAINS[ci];
      if (step < c.hands.length - 1) {
        step++;
        placeToken();
        $('relay-cap').innerHTML = c.hands[step].cap;
      }
      if (step === c.hands.length - 1) {
        $('relay-pass').classList.add('hidden');
        $('relay-qtext').textContent = c.q;
        $('relay-opts').innerHTML = c.opts.map((o, i) => `<button class="opt" data-i="${i}">${o}</button>`).join('');
        $('relay-q').classList.remove('hidden');
        ($('relay-opts').firstElementChild as HTMLElement).focus();
      }
    });
    $('relay-opts').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      const b = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLButtonElement>('.opt');
      if (!b || b.disabled) return;
      const c = CHAINS[ci];
      const pick = Number(b.dataset.i);
      const btns = [...$('relay-opts').querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.opt')];
      btns.forEach((x, i) => { x.disabled = true; if (i === c.ans) x.classList.add('ok'); });
      if (pick === c.ans) score.relay++;
      else b.classList.add('bad');
      $('relay-fb').innerHTML = (pick === c.ans ? good(c.why) : miss(c.why)) + `<p class="mt-1 text-sm">${link(c.ref)}</p>`;
      const next = $('relay-next');
      next.textContent = ci < CHAINS.length - 1 ? 'Next chain ▸' : 'On to the lock ▸';
      next.classList.remove('hidden');
      next.focus();
    });
    $('relay-next').addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (ci < CHAINS.length - 1) { ci++; loadChain(); return; }
      done.relay = true;
      $('relay-next').classList.add('hidden');
      $('relay-title').textContent = `Relay: ${score.relay}/${CHAINS.length} holders named`;
      $('relay-cap').textContent = 'Every chain ran out. On to Rav Naḥman\'s double ruling.';
      $('p3').scrollIntoView({ behavior: matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches ? 'auto' : 'smooth' });
      checkFinale();
    });
    loadChain();

    // =============== PART III: the lock ===============
    const REASONS = [
      { id: 'stands', t: 'the lambs stand already set apart, so the kohen grandfather could simply have declared his own lambs the redemption' },
      { id: 'itself', t: 'the gifts can be separated from the pile itself, which is lying right there' },
      { id: 'gift', t: 'anything that came to a kohen as a gift is exempt from tithe' },
      { id: 'gentile', t: 'he comes in the place of a man the kohen can\'t take to court' },
    ];
    const ANS = { a: 'stands', b: 'itself' };
    const sel: Record<'a' | 'b', string | null> = { a: null, b: null };
    let lockMissed = false;
    (['a', 'b'] as const).forEach((k) => {
      const box = $(`dial-${k}`);
      box.innerHTML = REASONS.map((r) => `<button class="opt text-sm" role="radio" aria-checked="false" data-id="${r.id}">${r.t}</button>`).join('');
      box.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
        const b = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLButtonElement>('.opt');
        if (!b || done.lock) return;
        sel[k] = b.dataset.id!;
        box.querySelectorAll('.opt').forEach((x) => { x.setAttribute('aria-checked', String(x === b)); x.classList.remove('bad'); });
      });
    });
    $('lock-try').addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (done.lock) return;
      if (!sel.a || !sel.b) { $('lock-fb').innerHTML = miss('Set both dials first.'); return; }
      const okA = sel.a === ANS.a, okB = sel.b === ANS.b;
      if (okA && okB) {
        done.lock = true;
        score.lock = lockMissed ? 0 : 1;
        $('lock-icon').textContent = '🔓';
        document.querySelectorAll('#dial-a .opt, #dial-b .opt').forEach((x) => { if (x.getAttribute('aria-checked') === 'true') x.classList.add('ok'); });
        $('lock-fb').innerHTML = good(
          'Open. <strong>Donkeys alone:</strong> maybe only there, because the lambs "stand separated" (<span dir="rtl" lang="he">מַפְרַישׁ וְקָאֵי</span>). But grain gifts must be separated and declared, and "gifts not separated are as if not separated," so the kohen never acquired them. <strong>Grain alone:</strong> maybe only there, because you can tithe the pile from itself, while a donkey needs a lamb brought from elsewhere. Each case has its own reason, so both rulings were needed.',
        ) + `<p class="mt-1 text-sm">${link('Bekhorot 11a:23')} · ${link('Bekhorot 11a:25')}</p>`;
        checkFinale();
        return;
      }
      lockMissed = true;
      (['a', 'b'] as const).forEach((k) => {
        if (sel[k] !== ANS[k]) $(`dial-${k}`).querySelector(`[aria-checked="true"]`)?.classList.add('bad');
      });
      $('lock-fb').innerHTML = miss(
        `${okA ? '' : 'The donkey dial is wrong: what is special about lambs, as opposed to grain gifts that still need separating? '}${okB ? '' : 'The grain dial is wrong: what does grain have that a donkey, needing a lamb from outside, lacks? '}`,
      );
    });

    // =============== finale ===============
    function checkFinale() {
      if (!(done.purse && done.relay && done.lock)) return;
      const total = score.purse + score.relay + score.lock;
      const max = ROUNDS.length + CHAINS.length + 1;
      $('finale-text').innerHTML = `${total}/${max}. "From the moment he set it aside, it stands in the kohen's possession." Even a lamb that never reached the kohen's hand was already his.`;
      $('finale').classList.remove('hidden');
    }
  </script>
</Layout>
